// BUG (filed by v-core-opt 2026-07-20): a SELF-TAIL-RECURSIVE function whose innermost match is MIXED
// (a recursive arm beside a VALUE-RETURNING arm) and whose recursive arm returns an OPTION-typed value
// emits INVALID WASM under the tail-loop conversion (select.rs): `func N failed to validate: type mismatch,
// values remaining on stack at end of block`. The `br` (loop-continue) from the recursive arm leaves the
// enclosing `if (result i32)` stack-unbalanced. NON-CONST — this is NOT const-specialization (v-core-opt's
// const-param-drop fix is separate + validated); it reproduces with a PLAIN `step` param, so it is the
// wasm tail-loop conversion's handling of a mixed-match recursive arm. LIKELY v-wasm-opt lane (select.rs
// tail-loop / `emit_tail`). Blocks v-iterators' filter-map (whose keep=return / drop=recurse shape is
// exactly this mixed-match tail recursion), independently of the const-param-drop bug.
//
// REPRO: `cdz compile` this -> `func 20 failed to validate`. A SCALAR-returning variant (None => 0,
// Some => y instead of building Options) COMPILES + RUNS -> so the trigger is the Option-typed recursive
// tail arm in a mixed match, not the recursion itself.

type Iter = | Mk(List(Int64), List(Int64) -> Option((Int64, List(Int64))))
def from-list(xs) = Iter.Mk(xs, fn(s) => match s with
  | [] => Option.None(unit) | [h, .. t] => Option.Some((h, t)))
def classify(x: Int64) = if x > 2 then Option.Some(x) else Option.None(unit)
def twostep(step: List(Int64) -> Option((Int64, List(Int64))), s: List(Int64)) =
  match step(s) with
  | Option.None(_) => Option.None(unit)
  | Option.Some(pair) => (match pair with | (x, s2) =>
    (match classify(x) with
     | Option.None(_) => twostep(step, s2)
     | Option.Some(y) => Option.Some((y, s2))))
def run2(it) = match it with | Iter.Mk(s0, step) => twostep(step, s0)
def main() = run2(from-list([1,2,3,4]))
export { main }

// ===== TRIAGE (corpus-bugfix, 2026-07-20) =====
// RESOLVED — no longer reproduces on current trunk base. `cdz compile` now succeeds (wrote 3204 bytes,
// no "func N failed to validate") and `cdz run` computes the correct value:
//   (Some (tuple 3 (list 4))) : Option((Int64, List(Int64)))  — filters x>2 from [1,2,3,4].
// The mixed-match Option-typed recursive tail arm no longer leaves the enclosing if(result i32) stack
// unbalanced under the tail-loop conversion (select.rs / emit_tail). This is the NON-CONST twin of the
// const-fn-param-drop repro (also RESOLVED this tick) — together they were v-iterators' filter-map
// blocker; both fixed. Marked RESOLVED.
